 "sq": [
  {
   "_id": 18187,
   "ANSWER": "<p>Multicore programming enables operating systems to <strong data-end=\"1782\" data-start=\"1760\">maximize CPU usage</strong> by executing multiple processes or threads in parallel, leading to <strong data-end=\"1895\" data-start=\"1850\">better performance, faster response times</strong>, and <strong data-end=\"1927\" data-start=\"1901\">efficient multitasking</strong>.</p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC202J",
   "LEVEL": 2,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1",
    "PLO2"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<h3 data-end=\"1694\" data-start=\"1614\"><strong data-end=\"1692\" data-start=\"1618\">Why is multicore programming important in modern operating systems?</strong></h3>\n\n<p data-end=\"1928\" data-start=\"1695\">&nbsp;</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 206,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 18187
  },
  {
   "_id": 18250,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"1931\" data-start=\"1918\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ol data-end=\"2154\" data-start=\"1932\">\n\t<li data-end=\"2040\" data-start=\"1932\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2040\" data-start=\"1935\"><strong data-end=\"1963\" data-start=\"1935\">Improved responsiveness:</strong> Threads can handle tasks like user input and background work concurrently.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"2154\" data-start=\"2041\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2154\" data-start=\"2044\"><strong data-end=\"2068\" data-start=\"2044\">Efficient CPU usage:</strong> Threads keep the CPU busy by switching between tasks during I/O operations or delays.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ol>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC202J",
   "LEVEL": 2,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1",
    "PLO2",
    "PLO3"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<h3 data-end=\"1917\" data-start=\"1860\"><strong data-end=\"1915\" data-start=\"1864\">Name two advantages of using multithreading.</strong></h3>\n\n<p data-end=\"1928\" data-start=\"1695\">&nbsp;</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 206,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 18250
  }
 ],
 "lq": [
  {
   "_id": 18251,
   "ANSWER": "<h3 data-end=\"2425\" data-start=\"2404\"><strong data-end=\"2423\" data-start=\"2408\">Definition:</strong></h3>\n\n<p data-end=\"2648\" data-start=\"2426\">Multithreading is a feature of operating systems where <strong data-end=\"2518\" data-start=\"2481\">multiple threads run concurrently</strong> within a single process. Threads share the same code, data, and system resources but operate independently in terms of execution.</p>\n\n<h3 data-end=\"2690\" data-start=\"2655\"><strong data-end=\"2690\" data-start=\"2659\">Benefits of Multithreading:</strong></h3>\n\n<ol data-end=\"3091\" data-start=\"2692\">\n\t<li data-end=\"2773\" data-start=\"2692\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2773\" data-start=\"2695\"><strong data-end=\"2716\" data-start=\"2695\">Faster Execution:</strong> Threads run in parallel, improving task completion time.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"2892\" data-start=\"2774\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2892\" data-start=\"2777\"><strong data-end=\"2806\" data-start=\"2777\">Increased Responsiveness:</strong> In GUI applications, one thread can handle UI while another handles background tasks.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"2988\" data-start=\"2893\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2988\" data-start=\"2896\"><strong data-end=\"2917\" data-start=\"2896\">Resource Sharing:</strong> Threads use less memory than processes since they share address space.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3091\" data-start=\"2989\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3091\" data-start=\"2992\"><strong data-end=\"3022\" data-start=\"2992\">Efficient CPU Utilization:</strong> Threads can run while others wait (e.g., for I/O), keeping CPU busy.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3 data-end=\"3133\" data-start=\"3098\"><strong data-end=\"3133\" data-start=\"3102\">Key Components of a Thread:</strong></h3>\n\n<ul data-end=\"3358\" data-start=\"3135\">\n\t<li data-end=\"3187\" data-start=\"3135\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3187\" data-start=\"3137\"><strong data-end=\"3151\" data-start=\"3137\">Thread ID:</strong> Unique identifier for each thread</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3246\" data-start=\"3188\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3246\" data-start=\"3190\"><strong data-end=\"3210\" data-start=\"3190\">Program Counter:</strong> Points to the current instruction</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3293\" data-start=\"3247\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3293\" data-start=\"3249\"><strong data-end=\"3263\" data-start=\"3249\">Registers:</strong> CPU register set per thread</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3358\" data-start=\"3294\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3358\" data-start=\"3296\"><strong data-end=\"3306\" data-start=\"3296\">Stack:</strong> Separate for each thread to manage function calls</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p data-end=\"3402\" data-start=\"3360\"><strong data-end=\"3402\" data-start=\"3360\">Shared by threads in the same process:</strong></p>\n\n<ul data-end=\"3451\" data-start=\"3403\">\n\t<li data-end=\"3419\" data-start=\"3403\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3419\" data-start=\"3405\">Code segment</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3436\" data-start=\"3420\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3436\" data-start=\"3422\">Data segment</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3451\" data-start=\"3437\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3451\" data-start=\"3439\">Open files</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 data-end=\"3495\" data-start=\"3458\"><strong data-end=\"3495\" data-start=\"3462\">Challenges in Multithreading:</strong></h3>\n\n<ol data-end=\"3859\" data-start=\"3497\">\n\t<li data-end=\"3596\" data-start=\"3497\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3596\" data-start=\"3500\"><strong data-end=\"3520\" data-start=\"3500\">Race Conditions:</strong> Two threads accessing shared data simultaneously can cause inconsistencies.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3672\" data-start=\"3597\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3672\" data-start=\"3600\"><strong data-end=\"3614\" data-start=\"3600\">Deadlocks:</strong> Threads waiting on each other indefinitely for resources.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3760\" data-start=\"3673\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3760\" data-start=\"3676\"><strong data-end=\"3701\" data-start=\"3676\">Debugging Difficulty:</strong> Errors are harder to reproduce and fix in concurrent code.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3859\" data-start=\"3761\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3859\" data-start=\"3764\"><strong data-end=\"3795\" data-start=\"3764\">Context Switching Overhead:</strong> Still involves some CPU overhead for switching between threads.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3 data-end=\"3893\" data-start=\"3866\"><strong data-end=\"3893\" data-start=\"3870\">Real-World Example:</strong></h3>\n\n<ul data-end=\"4128\" data-start=\"3895\">\n\t<li data-end=\"4034\" data-start=\"3895\">\n\t<p data-end=\"4034\" data-start=\"3897\"><strong data-end=\"3912\" data-start=\"3897\">Web Server:</strong> Each client request is handled by a separate thread. While one waits for database access, others can continue processing.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"4128\" data-start=\"4035\">\n\t<p data-end=\"4128\" data-start=\"4037\"><strong data-end=\"4053\" data-start=\"4037\">Text Editor:</strong> One thread handles user typing, while another handles background autosave.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 data-end=\"4156\" data-start=\"4135\"><strong data-end=\"4154\" data-start=\"4139\">Conclusion:</strong></h3>\n\n<p data-end=\"4414\" data-start=\"4157\">Multithreading is a powerful mechanism in modern operating systems that improves <strong data-end=\"4294\" data-start=\"4238\">performance, responsiveness, and resource efficiency</strong>. However, it requires careful design to <strong data-end=\"4363\" data-start=\"4335\">avoid concurrency issues</strong> and to <strong data-end=\"4393\" data-start=\"4371\">synchronize access</strong> to shared resources.</p>\n",
